From: Christopher Obbard <obbardc@debian.org>
Date: Sun, 12 Apr 2026 06:26:55 +0100
Subject: debian/patches: drop Windows-only pyo3 generate-import-lib
 dependency

Remove the upstream cfg(windows) pyo3 dependency enabling the
generate-import-lib feature when generating Cargo.lock for the Debian
package.

This feature is only needed for Windows cross-compilation with maturin
and is not required for Debian Linux builds. Keeping it causes
cargo generate-lockfile --offline to fail during dependency resolution
in Debian even though the dependency is Windows-only.

Forwarded: not-needed
Signed-off-by: Christopher Obbard <obbardc@debian.org>
---
 Cargo.toml | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Cargo.toml b/Cargo.toml
index 3de5879..ea8167e 100644
--- a/Cargo.toml
+++ b/Cargo.toml
@@ -24,8 +24,8 @@ cpufeatures = "0.2"
 # and macOS builds. pyo3 main has deprecated this feature in favor of
 # raw-dylib linking — revisit once that ships in a pyo3 release and maturin
 # drops the stale interpreter-presence check.
-[target.'cfg(windows)'.dependencies]
-pyo3 = { version = "0.28", features = ["generate-import-lib"] }
+#[target.'cfg(windows)'.dependencies]
+#pyo3 = { version = "0.28", features = ["generate-import-lib"] }
 
 
 [profile.release]
